        "original_id": "3ff6d386-fa20-580c-b0d9-9931f26060ce",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: WWF The Music, Vol. 5\n- Companies: WWE, World Wrestling Federation, Koch Records\n- People: Jim Johnston\n- Bands: Motörhead\n- Topics: soundtrack albums, wrestling entrance theme music\n\nFacts:\n- Jim Johnston is an American music composer born in 1959.\n- Jim Johnston is best known for his work with WWE, formerly the World Wrestling Federation, beginning in 1985.\n- WWF The Music, Vol. 5 is a soundtrack album by WWE, then known as the World Wrestling Federation.\n- Koch Records released WWF The Music, Vol. 5 on February 20, 2001.\n- WWF The Music, Vol. 5 features entrance theme music for various WWE superstars.\n- Jim Johnston composed and performed all of the music on WWF The Music, Vol. 5 except for one song performed by Motörhead.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
